{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-19T00:19:32.036Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"928e5cd9a3bda9591c204f9f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.327","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1754"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1754: cursor-named fields inside items block string compaction, so a budgeted list omits its rows (regression since 2026.11.11)"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Reported in GH-1754 against 2026.11.18. The protection that keeps emitted continuation tokens replayable also exempts item fields that merely share a continuation key name (next_cursor, output_cursor) from string compaction. At a 2,000-token budget, a list whose one item carries a 30,000-character next_cursor or output_cursor field exits 2 with read_output.result_omitted true and strings_compacted false. The same request on 2026.11.11 returned one compacted row and exited 0. An ordinary_text control still compacts to a 255-character value. Only the envelope's continuation tokens should be exempt; the cursor-clipping fix is related."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:output","compaction","gh:1754","output-budget","read-output","regression"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-19T00:19:32.036Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-19T00:19:32.036Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":150},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A budgeted list whose item carries an oversized next_cursor or output_cursor field returns its compacted row and exits 0; An envelope next_cursor or output_cursor is still delivered intact and replays; Tests cover both the replayable envelope cursor and compaction of cursor-named item metadata"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5t33or"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Producer and output continuation tokens in the response envelope stay replayable, while oversized strings under items, including fields named like a continuation key, are still compacted so the budgeted list returns its rows."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"An item field named next_cursor or output_cursor is exempt from compaction, so at a 2,000-token budget the list is omitted (result_omitted true, strings_compacted false, exit 2) instead of returning a compacted row as 2026.11.11 did."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1710","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-19T00:19:32.036Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"224e9488f4a2e8554ebfd3fdd80a365e646b4683ae37fea211a887a5c9a79fdb","item_hash_version":3,"message":"File GH-1754","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"8fc8e7ed7d0bd39be1035b7f58f1afe724faf16559c84bf152603570c805f775"}
